  "response": "Read the four call sites in the fixture. Here's the proposal.\n\n## The finding\n\n`crime_00064` — `duplicate_component_shape`, medium/0.7, four occurrences of the same `<div>` subtree:\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |\n\nThe subtree is the form action bar. I diffed all four: they are byte-identical except for the submit label.\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>   {/* ← \"Edit Invoice\" in the edit forms */}\n</div>\n```\n\nOne varying token across four copies, and eight lines of hand-maintained Tailwind — including the `h-10`/`px-4` sizing that has to stay visually matched to `<Button>`. That's the drift surface: a hover state, a focus ring, or an `aria-disabled` added to one copy silently leaves the other three behind.\n\n## Scope constraint worth stating up front\n\n`final-example` and `starter-example` are two independent Next.js apps (separate `app/` trees, each resolving its own `@/` alias). They're a tutorial's before/after pair, so their divergence is deliberate — consolidating *across* them would need a shared package and would defeat the fixture's purpose. So this is **the same extraction performed twice, once per app**, each covering its own create/edit pair. Within an app it's a 2-call-site dedupe; the \"4 files\" in the finding is really 2 × 2.\n\n## Shared component\n\n`app/ui/form-actions.tsx` — one per app, presentational, no hooks, so it works in either a Server or Client Component:\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  submitDisabled = false,\n  children,\n}: FormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" aria-disabled={submitDisabled}>\n        {submitLabel}\n      </Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Public API**\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cancelHref` | `string` | *(required)* | Identical in all four today, but hardcoding it makes the component un-reusable outside invoices for no gain. |\n| `submitLabel` | `string` | *(required)* | The only thing that actually differs. No default — a wrong-but-plausible default is exactly how \"Create Invoice\" ends up on an edit form. |\n| `cancelLabel` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Defaulted; overridable for \"Discard\" / \"Back\". |\n| `submitDisabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Not used by current call sites. Include it — `useActionState` pending state is the next thing anyone adds, and adding it later means touching every copy again, which is the failure this extraction exists to prevent. |\n\n**Slots**\n\n- `children` — extra actions rendered **left** of Cancel, so the primary/secondary ordering stays fixed. This is where a Delete Invoice or Save Draft button goes without anyone reaching for the layout classes.\n\n**Deliberately not props:** `className` on the wrapper, and anything controlling the Link's styling. Those are the drift vector. If the action bar needs a second variant, add a named `variant` prop with enumerated cases rather than an open string — an open `className` re-opens exactly the hole this closes.\n\n## Files that change\n\nPer app (×2):\n\n1. **New:** `app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n2. `app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` — replace the 9-line footer with `<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />`; drop the now-unused `Link` import if nothing else in the file uses it (it doesn't in either app's create-form).\n3. `app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` — same, `submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\"`.\n\n**6 files total: 2 new, 4 edited.** Effort matches the finding's `small`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `Button` is itself flagged as an exact duplicate across the two apps (`crime_00043`) — same cross-app boundary, same reason to leave it alone.\n- The `design_token_escape` findings on these four files (`crime_00072/73/76/77`, the `18px`/`14px` values) sit in the *field* markup higher up, not in this subtree. This refactor doesn't touch them; they're a separate pass.\n- Verification is visual — there are no tests in the fixture. Diff the rendered create and edit pages before/after; the extraction should be a pure no-op apart from the added `aria-disabled=\"false\"` attribute.",
